Polished finance narrative (ready to read or paste into slides)
“Metro Manufacturing finished the last quarter with $1.8M in revenue and $2.1M in cash on hand. Our current operating profile shows a modest net cash burn (~$72K/month), which gives us a healthy buffer to fund operations and planned initiatives. At our reported burn level, we maintain multi-quarter runway, allowing us to prioritize growth investments in production capacity and sales coverage while preserving optionality. We recommend the board approve the proposed near-term investments conditional on hitting quarterly revenue and margin milestones; in parallel we will implement tighter receivables monitoring and scenario-based contingency plans to preserve optionality.”

Key financial highlights to show the board
- Cash: $2.1M
- Last quarter revenue: $1.8M (annualized ≈ $7.2M)
- Monthly burn: $72K (clarify net vs gross)
- Simple runway (cash / burn): ~29 months (or 20 months if adjusted — reconcile)
- Immediate priority metrics: gross margin %, AR days, customer concentration (top 5 customers % of revenue), backlog or contracted revenue.

Top risks (ranked) and suggested mitigations
1) Revenue shortfall / demand shock
   - Why: Quarter-to-quarter revenue can be lumpy; large customers or seasonality could reduce near-term receipts.
   - Impact: Reduced cash inflow shortens runway quickly.
   - Mitigations: tighten sales pipeline visibility (weekly updates), accelerate small-win channels, prioritize converting backlog, prepare a 3-scenario forecast (base / downside / stretch) showing cash impact and trigger points for action.

2) Customer concentration
   - Why: If a few customers make up a large share of revenue, losing one is high-impact.
   - Impact: Abrupt revenue decline, bad debt risk.
   - Mitigations: diversify pipeline, negotiate longer-term contracts, add payment protections (deposits / milestone billing), increase DSO monitoring.

3) Receivables and working capital tightness
   - Why: Long AR days can create temporary cash squeezes even when revenue is healthy.
   - Impact: Narrows available cash, could force borrowing or slowed production.
   - Mitigations: shorten payment terms, offer small early-payment discounts, tighten credit approvals, consider invoice financing as contingency.

4) Margin compression (cost increases or price pressure)
   - Why: Raw material or freight inflation or competitive pricing pressure.
   - Impact: Gross margin fall leads to higher net burn.
   - Mitigations: pass-through pricing clauses, supplier renegotiation, operational efficiency projects; model margin sensitivity scenarios.

5) One-time / committed spend (capex, legal, debt)
   - Why: Contracted investments or debt payments reduce available cash.
   - Impact: Can materially reduce runway if unbudgeted.
   - Mitigations: map all committed obligations, rephase non-critical capex, prioritize projects with quick payback, negotiate payment terms.

6) Talent retention / execution risk
   - Why: Losing key ops/sales staff delays growth and raises costs.
   - Impact: Slower revenue, increased hiring costs.
   - Mitigations: retention incentives, succession planning, selective hiring tied to milestones.

7) Macroeconomic / supply chain risk
   - Why: Supplier disruptions raise unit costs; demand may slow.
   - Impact: Production delays, margin compression.
   - Mitigations: multi-sourcing, inventory buffers for critical items, hedging where appropriate.

Recommended board asks and decisions
- Approve the near-term growth funding (amount and conditions) with clear KPIs and quarterly review.
- Approve scenario-planning: board sign-off on a pre-defined contingency if revenue falls below X% of plan (e.g., reduce discretionary spend by Y%, pause hires).
- Authorize management to negotiate short-term financing line (small facility) for working capital as a backup (only draw if downside triggers occur).

Suggested slides / one-page structure (for brevity in the board packet)
1. One-line financial snapshot (cash, runway, last quarter revenue, burn)
2. Key trends & drivers (growth, churn, margin)
3. Executive recommendation & asks
4. Risk register (top 5 risks with mitigations & triggers)
5. 3-scenario cash forecast (base / downside / upside for next 12 months)

