  - Mitigations: Tighten payment terms for new contracts, accelerate invoicing, offer early-pay discounts, increase collections cadence, monitor AR aging weekly.

- Risk: Understated burn (planned hires, product investments, capex)
  - Impact: Actual runway materially shorter than stated.
  - Mitigations: Reconcile forecast to include all headcount and one-time spends; run a 0/6/12/24 month forecast; require approvals for hires over X cost.

- Risk: Macroeconomic / customer demand shock
  - Impact: Revenue reduction, delayed orders.
  - Mitigations: Create 3 scenario forecasts (base, -20% revenue, -40% revenue) and contingency actions for each (cost deferrals, hiring freeze triggers).

- Risk: Supply chain or manufacturing disruption
  - Impact: Inability to deliver, revenue loss, additional costs.
  - Mitigations: Identify single-source suppliers, build safety stock for critical components, renegotiate lead times, and quantify worst-case costs.

- Risk: Margin pressure (material, labor inflation)
  - Impact: Higher burn and lower gross margin.
  - Mitigations: Price reviews, product mix optimization, pass-through clauses where possible.

- Risk: Covenant / financing constraints (if any debt exists)
  - Impact: Forced renegotiation or liquidity shortfall.
  - Mitigations: Review covenants now, stress test covenant compliance for next 12 months, engage lenders early if at risk.

