   - Revenue growth/decline, one-time expenses, large contracts, capex or debt changes
4. Immediate asks/decisions for the board
   - Approval for contingency plan / hiring freeze thresholds / authority to raise bridge financing
5. Recommended action plan (next 90 days)
   - Validate runway assumptions; run scenario analysis
   - Strengthen cash collection (AR), push/accelerate high-margin revenue
   - Short-term cost controls and prioritization of highest ROI spend
6. Risks & mitigations (next section)

Key risks (prioritized) with suggested mitigations
1. Revenue shock / customer loss (High impact, Medium likelihood)
   - Why it matters: Revenue drives cash generation; losing a top customer could materially shorten runway.
   - Mitigations: Diversify top customers, lock renewals/POs with favorable payment terms, accelerate sales pipeline, offer short-term incentives to retain large customers.

2. Cash-flow timing (AR delays, seasonal receipts) (High impact, Medium-high likelihood)
   - Why: Even if runway looks healthy, slow collections can create short-term crunches.
   - Mitigations: Tighten credit terms, daily/weekly AR reporting, offer early-pay discounts, securitize receivables or draw on a credit line.

