   - Mitigations: maintain minimum liquidity threshold (e.g., $X), keep a line of credit option or convertible bridge ready.
6) Talent & execution risk (key hires delayed or not hired)
   - Mitigations: freeze non-essential hiring, reallocate internal resources to critical projects, use contractors for short-term needs.
7) Financing conditions / covenant risk if borrowing
   - Mitigations: run covenant stress tests in scenarios, negotiate flexible covenants, prioritize conservative leverage targets.

