Metro Manufacturing enters the board period with $2.1M of liquidity and $1.8M revenue last quarter. At the reported net cash burn of $72K/month, our liquidity supports roughly 29 months of runway; if our net burn is instead ~$105K/month, runway is ~20 months. Revenue remains the primary driver of cash generation; we are focused on sustaining top-line momentum while managing discretionary spend and optimizing working capital. Key decisions requested from the board: confirm fundraising posture (timing/target), endorse contingency cost actions if revenue softens, and approve investment in high-return product initiatives.

Top risks and suggested mitigations
