  - Risk: Raw material or freight cost increases reduce gross margin.
  - Mitigation: Pass-through pricing where possible, renegotiate supplier contracts, hedge or bulk buy critical inputs.
  - Owner: COO + Procurement
- Working capital & receivables (medium)
  - Risk: Increasing DSO ties up cash.
  - Mitigation: Tighten credit terms, incentives for early payment, AR financing if needed.
  - Owner: Finance Manager
- Supply chain or production disruptions (medium)
  - Risk: Lead-time increases or supplier failures create stockouts and lost revenue.
  - Mitigation: Secondary suppliers, safety stock for critical items, production contingency plan.
  - Owner: Supply Chain Lead
- Talent / execution risk (medium)
  - Risk: Key hires or retention issues affecting delivery of growth projects.
  - Mitigation: Key person retention plans, hiring prioritization, outsourcing non-core tasks.
  - Owner: Head of HR / CEO
- Fundraising / liquidity timing (medium)
  - Risk: Market conditions or execution delays reduce access to capital when needed.
  - Mitigation: Pre-lay groundwork with investors, maintain a 9–12 month “runway cushion” target, consider bridge options.
  - Owner: CFO + CEO

