- Metro Manufacturing enters the board period with $2.1M cash, last quarter revenue of $1.8M, and reported monthly net burn of $72K (please confirm definition). Based on those figures, we have multi-quarter runway and flexibility to execute near-term growth initiatives while retaining optionality on external financing. Near-term priorities are protecting gross margins, reducing working-capital risk (AR/inventory), and sequencing hires/investments so we preserve 18–24+ months of runway under downside scenarios. We recommend the board approve a focused cash-preservation contingency and a minimal financing plan to de-risk outstanding capacity investments.

